a52sxq: keep the /dev/ipa and /dev/wwan_ioctl UAPI at the 5.4 layout (audit 2026-11-18)

The vendor ipacm/libipanat are built with the 5.4 msm_ipa.h. The ioctl numbers
carry pointer types, so nothing rejected the r30 layout: ADD_HDR/COPY_HDR
copied 308/296-byte entries over 120/108-byte user structs, every struct that
embeds ipa_rule_attrib (rt/flt rules, tx/rx props) was 12 bytes short, the V2
rule ioctls returned -EPERM, events from 48 up were shifted by one and
WAN_IOCTL_NOTIFY_NAT_MOVE_RES was 22 instead of 21.

 - IPA_HDR_MAX_SIZE 64; ipa_rule_attrib tail p_exception + fld_val_eq;
   ipa_hdr_proc_ctx_add tail generic_params_v2 + gre_params (and the 5.4 bit
   names in the eogre/eth_II_ex params); ipa_wlan_msg.ast_update;
   ipa_wlan_hdr_attrib_val.u.ta_peer_id; ipa_ioc_vlan_iface_info.vlan_id
   __u16; ipa_pdn_ip_collision_cfg.vlan_id; 5.4 ipa_ioc_ext_router_info.
 - 5.4 event values from IPA_SW_FLT_EVENT on (DONE_RESTORE and ETH_PDU slots
   kept); the r30-only IPA_WARNING_LIMIT_REACHED moves behind them (59).
 - IPA_IOCTL_SET_EXT_ROUTER_MODE 95; r30-only ioctls 94/95/96 -> 100/101/102.
 - WAN_IOCTL_NOTIFY_NAT_MOVE_RES 21, SET_DATA_QUOTA_WARNING 21 -> 23.
 - ipa.c: static_asserts for the sizes/offsets confirmed in the ipacm binary.

Checked by drivers612/conn/data/abi-check.py (run by build.sh) against
abi54/linux; the remaining differences are listed in abi54/EXCEPTIONS.

